WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.836
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.106 --> 00:03.108
[♪ opening theme song plays]

3
00:43.065 --> 00:48.070
THE PERFECT LIE

4
00:53.158 --> 00:54.868
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION

5
00:54.951 --> 00:58.080
SCENES INVOLVING CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY

6
00:58.163 --> 01:05.128
HOUSE OF GRACE

7
01:05.212 --> 01:06.630
[♪ foreboding strings build]

8
01:16.139 --> 01:18.058
[Junho] The house where my wife was born and raised.

9
01:18.141 --> 01:19.768
POSTS dr.min.jh

10
01:20.519 --> 01:23.063
My mother-in-law always welcomes me with open arms.

11
01:24.731 --> 01:27.818
[♪ unsettling music plays]

12
01:52.175 --> 01:54.845
Have some. You've come such a long way.

13
01:54.928 --> 01:57.848
-Thank you. -No problem. [chuckles]

14
01:58.807 --> 01:59.808
[Junho's mother-in-law] So…

15
02:00.559 --> 02:03.937
how did you say you knew Eunhye?

16
02:05.147 --> 02:10.735
Oh, I've never actually met Ms. Joo Eunhye.

17
02:11.403 --> 02:12.404
I…

18
02:13.405 --> 02:15.574
know Mr. Min Junho and Hyunsoo.

19
02:16.158 --> 02:17.576
I see.

20
02:18.118 --> 02:20.537
Please, have a seat.

21
02:27.711 --> 02:30.005
Your daughter was very beautiful.

22
02:32.466 --> 02:33.675
Yes, she was.

23
02:34.301 --> 02:35.761
She had such a gentle heart too.

24
02:43.435 --> 02:45.687
[Jisun] Looks like your daughter liked to cook too.

25
02:46.354 --> 02:48.273
[Eunhye's mom] The friend next to her is a chef.

26
02:49.149 --> 02:53.862
They grew up in the same neighborhood and were inseparable even into adulthood.

27
02:55.113 --> 02:58.325
They even opened a restaurant together,

28
02:59.326 --> 03:02.704
but Eunhye left when she got married.

29
03:03.914 --> 03:04.915
Why?

30
03:05.665 --> 03:09.544
Running a business just wasn't for her.

31
03:09.628 --> 03:11.838
Her dream was to be a traditional wife and mother.

32
03:12.839 --> 03:13.882
I see.

33
03:15.801 --> 03:17.385
[Eunhye's mom chuckles softly]

34
03:17.469 --> 03:21.306
Well, anyway, what brings you here?

35
03:22.641 --> 03:23.683
Oh, well…

36
03:25.018 --> 03:27.062
I'm not sure how to say this…

37
03:27.145 --> 03:29.523
It's okay. Just tell me.

38
03:30.232 --> 03:31.900
You can be honest with me.

39
03:39.699 --> 03:43.495
Not long ago, Mr. Min Junho and I…

40
03:45.330 --> 03:46.831
went on a date.

41
03:52.045 --> 03:53.338
[sighs]

42
04:00.387 --> 04:01.471
[chuckles]

43
04:02.472 --> 04:03.473
That's good to hear.

44
04:10.564 --> 04:11.565
That night…

45
04:13.358 --> 04:15.235
it was raining really hard.

46
04:15.318 --> 04:17.237
[♪ tense music plays]

47
04:17.320 --> 04:20.824
So because of the rain that night,

48
04:20.907 --> 04:24.286
he came into my place while he was waiting for his taxi.

49
04:24.369 --> 04:26.121
[Eunhye's mom] Hold on. [clears throat]

50
04:27.372 --> 04:31.668
I'd rather not hear about the two of you.

51
04:31.751 --> 04:33.128
When the time is right…

52
04:35.380 --> 04:38.800
I'm sure he'll tell me himself.

53
04:44.764 --> 04:45.974
Actually…

54
04:53.565 --> 04:54.649
Never mind.

55
05:00.655 --> 05:04.868
I just want to know what Mr. Min was like back then.

56
05:09.706 --> 05:13.001
[Eunhye's mom] Junho was absolutely devoted to Eunhye.

57
05:13.084 --> 05:17.047
He couldn't have treated her any better.

58
05:19.758 --> 05:22.260
He was the best father to Hyunsoo,

59
05:23.053 --> 05:26.306
and he was a wonderful son-in-law to us too.

60
05:31.269 --> 05:34.981
Were he and Eunhye happy together throughout their marriage?

61
05:37.525 --> 05:39.194
[Eunhye's mom] He was always a family man,

62
05:39.277 --> 05:42.072
the kind of person who only had eyes for his wife.

63
05:43.448 --> 05:45.158
Even when Eunhye was sick…

64
05:54.793 --> 05:58.630
I heard your daughter had some unfortunate health issues.

65
06:03.051 --> 06:05.929
Could I ask if it got worse

66
06:06.012 --> 06:08.139
-after she got married? -[inhales sharply]

67
06:08.223 --> 06:11.601
[exhales sharply] I'd rather not talk about that anymore.

68
06:11.685 --> 06:13.687
But didn't you find it a little strange?

69
06:14.312 --> 06:15.814
I mean, her husband was a doctor,

70
06:15.897 --> 06:18.024
so for her to end up like that from an overdose…

71
06:20.568 --> 06:25.115
Are you implying my son-in-law did something to my daughter?

72
06:25.198 --> 06:28.451
-No, that's not what I… -[sighs]

73
06:32.414 --> 06:34.249
I'd like you to leave now.

74
06:48.722 --> 06:50.640
I'm sorry if I made you uncomfortable.

75
07:08.908 --> 07:09.909
[car locks]

76
07:14.414 --> 07:17.250
[footsteps approaching]

77
07:19.002 --> 07:21.004
[♪ sinister music plays]

78
07:23.173 --> 07:24.591
[door lock beeping]

79
07:31.431 --> 07:38.104
EPISODE 5 M

80
07:43.276 --> 07:46.362
[Eunhye's mom] Jeongmi runs a café in the theme park across the main road.

81
07:47.614 --> 07:49.741
I guess it must be doing pretty well

82
07:49.824 --> 07:52.285
if she's still in business after all these years.

83
07:54.621 --> 07:56.498
What's the place called?

84
07:57.999 --> 08:01.544
[Eunhye's mom] Dear My Friend, I think.

85
08:05.340 --> 08:06.508
[♪ ambient music plays]

86
08:09.093 --> 08:11.596
-[staff] Welcome. -Hello.

87
08:12.847 --> 08:14.265
Can I take your order?

88
08:15.225 --> 08:17.936
Could I ask if the owner here…

89
08:24.234 --> 08:25.610
Jeongmi?

90
08:30.448 --> 08:33.827
You can't believe Min Junho would do something like that, can you?

91
08:36.079 --> 08:37.080
[Jeongmi] But…

92
08:39.165 --> 08:42.502
I don't think you would've come all this way just to lie about it.

93
08:46.840 --> 08:50.051
But why did you come to see me?

94
08:52.929 --> 08:55.765
I came because I wanted to know more about Min Junho.

95
08:58.935 --> 09:00.937
And about Ms. Joo Eunhye too.

96
09:03.231 --> 09:04.232
Eunhye?

97
09:07.735 --> 09:11.656
I heard she died from an overdose.

98
09:13.825 --> 09:17.036
Eunhye suffered from depression.

99
09:19.622 --> 09:21.708
What was their marriage like?

100
09:25.670 --> 09:30.091
They were much happier than most couples.

101
09:31.759 --> 09:34.554
He was always so loving and devoted to her.

102
09:35.722 --> 09:38.057
It was almost touching.

103
09:38.141 --> 09:40.476
But Ms. Joo Eunhye wasn't happy, was she?

104
09:44.022 --> 09:46.191
Maybe there was a problem in their marriage

105
09:46.274 --> 09:47.734
that she couldn't talk about?

106
09:49.068 --> 09:50.111
[breathes shakily]

107
09:50.987 --> 09:53.239
-I don't think so-- -Was there ever anything

108
09:53.323 --> 09:55.158
that seemed strange or bothered you?

109
09:59.370 --> 10:00.496
No.

110
10:01.789 --> 10:04.292
You've known Eunhye since you were very young.

111
10:06.461 --> 10:08.796
Is there really nothing you can tell me?

112
10:09.380 --> 10:10.673
Oh, gosh.

113
10:11.466 --> 10:12.717
I'm sorry.

114
10:23.895 --> 10:26.689
If you think of anything at all, please call me anytime.

115
10:37.450 --> 10:40.453
[door opens, closes]

116
10:41.079 --> 10:42.330
[breathes shakily]

117
10:52.090 --> 10:53.675
[♪ ominous music plays]

118
10:53.758 --> 10:55.009
[sniffles]

119
10:55.093 --> 10:56.094
[water running]

120
11:01.891 --> 11:03.893
[♪ music intensifies]

121
11:28.042 --> 11:30.044
[♪ pensive music plays]

122
11:47.061 --> 11:49.022
[♪ music intensifies]

123
12:03.328 --> 12:04.329
[door unlocks]

124
12:11.169 --> 12:12.170
[door locks]

125
12:30.021 --> 12:31.022
[phone ringing]

126
12:58.216 --> 13:03.179
Before Eunhye died…

127
13:06.015 --> 13:08.226
Min Junho and I…

128
13:11.813 --> 13:14.440
slept together.

129
13:18.569 --> 13:22.490
[voice breaking] I'm not that kind of person.

130
13:24.200 --> 13:27.328
You have no idea how much the guilt has been eating me alive.

131
13:35.002 --> 13:38.131
All this time, I thought it was all my fault.

132
13:44.595 --> 13:47.390
You were drugged with GHB too, weren't you?

133
13:47.473 --> 13:50.601
-[breathes shakily] -[♪ ominous music plays]

134
13:50.685 --> 13:52.603
I think so.

135
13:54.021 --> 13:57.191
I felt sick all day the next day,

136
13:57.984 --> 14:00.486
and I couldn't remember anything.

137
14:02.738 --> 14:07.160
It was the biggest mistake of my life.

138
14:07.243 --> 14:09.287
[♪ music intensifies]

139
14:10.538 --> 14:12.790
[sighs] After all this time…

140
14:15.376 --> 14:17.253
It's pathetic, isn't it?

141
14:23.050 --> 14:24.677
It's the murder of the soul.

142
14:27.471 --> 14:28.681
You've been the victim

143
14:28.764 --> 14:30.975
of one of the most heinous and despicable crimes.

144
14:34.270 --> 14:36.898
Yet most victims believe that they are the ones at fault.

145
14:36.981 --> 14:38.858
[sobbing]

146
14:38.941 --> 14:41.986
They endlessly torture themselves with regret and blame.

147
14:42.069 --> 14:43.696
[wailing]

148
14:46.032 --> 14:49.619
Even after they realize what happened, very few ever report it.

149
14:50.661 --> 14:52.246
[♪ music intensifies]

150
14:56.417 --> 14:57.752
I was the same way.

151
15:03.674 --> 15:05.468
I don't know how, but…

152
15:07.803 --> 15:08.930
Eunhye…

153
15:11.891 --> 15:15.228
found out about what happened between Min Junho and me.

154
15:18.773 --> 15:19.941
And after that…

155
15:23.819 --> 15:25.613
Not long after…

156
15:27.323 --> 15:28.491
Eunhye…

157
15:34.830 --> 15:36.582
It wasn't your fault, Jeongmi.

158
15:36.666 --> 15:38.584
Eunhye must have also known the truth

159
15:38.668 --> 15:40.753
about what kind of person Min Junho really was.

160
15:44.423 --> 15:45.883
Come to Sangcheon with me.

161
15:46.467 --> 15:49.303
I hope you can go to the police and tell them the truth,

162
15:49.387 --> 15:53.015
and let people know what kind of person Min Junho really is.

163
15:54.308 --> 15:55.393
Okay.

164
15:55.893 --> 15:56.894
[sniffles]

165
15:59.939 --> 16:02.066
-Really? -Yes.

166
16:03.567 --> 16:05.403
I feel like it has to be done.

167
16:14.245 --> 16:17.164
[♪ music crescendos]

168
16:18.666 --> 16:19.667
[door opens]

169
16:21.294 --> 16:22.295
[music ends]

170
16:25.464 --> 16:26.465
ALL RECORDINGS

171
16:29.593 --> 16:32.096
KIM JEONGMI STATEMENT

172
16:35.391 --> 16:38.311
DETECTIVE LEE HWAYOUNG KIM JEONGMI STATEMENT.m4a

173
16:38.394 --> 16:39.395
[sighs]

174
17:03.169 --> 17:05.087
CALLING KIM JEONGMI

175
17:06.756 --> 17:08.883
[automated voice] The call cannot be connected.

176
17:08.966 --> 17:10.843
Please leave a message after the…

177
17:14.013 --> 17:15.181
[call connects]

178
17:15.264 --> 17:18.059
[automated voice] The call cannot be connected.

179
17:18.142 --> 17:21.228
Please leave a message after the beep.

180
17:21.312 --> 17:22.313
[call disconnects]

181
17:26.609 --> 17:27.610
[call connects]

182
17:27.693 --> 17:30.196
[line ringing]

183
17:30.905 --> 17:31.906
[phone buzzing]

184
17:44.710 --> 17:46.003
[buzzing continues]

185
17:47.046 --> 17:48.130
[♪ tense music plays]

186
17:48.214 --> 17:50.299
[phone buzzing]

187
17:54.553 --> 17:56.055
[heart monitor beeps steadily]

188
18:02.144 --> 18:06.148
[Junho] A good scalpel cuts so cleanly that it doesn't even leave a trace.

189
18:07.191 --> 18:08.442
Then, a moment later,

190
18:08.526 --> 18:11.320
a gasp of admiration bursts out at just how perfect the cut was.

191
18:14.031 --> 18:15.825
And that gasp comes in the form of blood.

192
18:16.867 --> 18:18.869
-[blood gurgling] -[phone buzzing]

193
18:26.043 --> 18:27.712
-Hello? -Sorry to call so early.

194
18:27.795 --> 18:29.338
Did you listen to the recording?

195
18:31.799 --> 18:33.134
What recording?

196
18:33.217 --> 18:34.760
I sent it last night.

197
18:35.970 --> 18:39.849
Min Junho used GHB to assault his late wife's friend too.

198
18:39.932 --> 18:41.267
The same method he used on me.

199
18:41.350 --> 18:45.521
Wait. You were supposed to keep your distance from Min Junho.

200
18:45.604 --> 18:48.858
We agreed to go to the police together, but now I can't get a hold of her.

201
18:49.650 --> 18:51.652
[♪ tense music plays]

202
18:53.195 --> 18:55.698
Let me listen to the recording first. I'll call you back.

203
18:57.533 --> 18:58.534
[call disconnects]

204
19:03.914 --> 19:07.084
[Jeongmi on recording] I felt sick all day the next day,

205
19:08.002 --> 19:10.421
and I couldn't remember anything.

206
19:11.172 --> 19:13.466
I thought it was just a hangover, but…

207
19:16.218 --> 19:20.723
It was the biggest mistake of my life.

208
19:25.269 --> 19:26.395
[Junho] Saw.

209
19:28.939 --> 19:30.941
-[saw whirring] -[phone buzzing]

210
19:32.610 --> 19:35.070
We have new evidence, so you can reinvestigate, right?

211
19:36.030 --> 19:37.406
This would open a new case.

212
19:38.365 --> 19:41.786
She can report it herself, but it isn't evidence that would justify

213
19:41.869 --> 19:43.662
reopening a previous investigation.

214
19:43.746 --> 19:44.914
That makes no sense.

215
19:44.997 --> 19:46.874
I wasn't Min Junho's first victim!

216
19:46.957 --> 19:49.043
[saw whirring]

217
19:49.126 --> 19:51.170
[Hwayoung] A recording of her statement isn't enough

218
19:51.253 --> 19:53.631
if she doesn't come forward herself. Besides…

219
19:55.424 --> 19:57.510
She doesn't have any evidence either, does she?

220
19:58.469 --> 20:00.387
[♪ tense music continues]

221
20:06.185 --> 20:07.394
[sighs softly]

222
20:11.357 --> 20:13.567
[groaning]

223
20:17.154 --> 20:19.281
[gagging]

224
20:22.076 --> 20:23.452
[retching]

225
20:25.204 --> 20:26.622
[Junho] Heart, please.

226
20:38.467 --> 20:40.594
[toilet flushes]

227
20:42.805 --> 20:44.390
[water running]

228
20:52.064 --> 20:53.941
[panting]

229
20:59.738 --> 21:01.198
[whimpers]

230
21:06.495 --> 21:08.581
[♪ ominous music plays]

231
21:09.957 --> 21:10.958
[gasps]

232
21:16.839 --> 21:19.049
[♪ chilling sting]

233
21:52.791 --> 21:54.418
[gasps, whimpers]

234
22:01.258 --> 22:03.510
[♪ ominous music plays]

235
22:23.864 --> 22:25.658
[obstetrician] You said you had some bleeding?

236
22:25.741 --> 22:26.992
Yes.

237
22:27.076 --> 22:28.827
I was fine until yesterday.

238
22:29.453 --> 22:31.205
[obstetrician] You're ten weeks pregnant.

239
22:31.872 --> 22:33.874
[chuckles] Don't worry.

240
22:33.958 --> 22:37.169
Some light bleeding is common at this stage of pregnancy.

241
22:37.795 --> 22:40.798
But I'm sure you're still worried, so let's take a look at the baby.

242
22:40.881 --> 22:42.841
-Yes, and for some reason… -[keyboard clacking]

243
22:44.051 --> 22:46.553
…I'm experiencing acute pain down there.

244
22:47.846 --> 22:49.682
[heartbeat pulsing]

245
22:49.765 --> 22:52.309
[obstetrician] See the heartbeat here?

246
22:52.393 --> 22:54.520
The baby's healthy and growing well.

247
22:54.603 --> 22:57.022
-[button clicks] -[glove snaps off]

248
22:58.315 --> 22:59.358
[sighs]

249
22:59.441 --> 23:01.443
I'll print out a copy for you.

250
23:01.527 --> 23:02.653
Thank you.

251
23:04.863 --> 23:08.283
Oh, and I noticed some abrasions inside.

252
23:08.367 --> 23:09.910
There are a few of them.

253
23:09.994 --> 23:12.371
They seem to be what's causing the bleeding and pain.

254
23:13.747 --> 23:15.416
That can't be…

255
23:16.083 --> 23:19.378
[obstetrician] Abrasions like that can sometimes happen during sex.

256
23:20.170 --> 23:22.756
They'll probably heal over time,

257
23:22.840 --> 23:25.759
but you might want to talk to your husband about it.

258
23:27.011 --> 23:28.012
No, I…

259
23:34.143 --> 23:35.269
[breathes shakily]

260
23:38.897 --> 23:39.898
I…

261
23:39.982 --> 23:41.150
[♪ unsettling music plays]

262
23:41.233 --> 23:43.235
I'd like to have some blood drawn, please.

263
23:47.406 --> 23:50.868
[♪ music builds]

264
24:37.998 --> 24:38.999
[door locks]

265
24:52.888 --> 24:54.681
[♪ tense music plays]

266
25:38.559 --> 25:40.686
[♪ music intensifies]

267
25:40.769 --> 25:42.354
SUNDAY

268
25:43.939 --> 25:45.899
[♪ chilling music plays]

269
25:53.323 --> 25:56.410
THURSDAY

270
26:06.003 --> 26:07.254
[call connects]

271
26:07.337 --> 26:08.422
Hey, it's me.

272
26:09.298 --> 26:11.550
Did you find out who the car is registered to?

273
26:11.633 --> 26:14.803
[detective] Oh. I called several times yesterday, but you--

274
26:14.887 --> 26:16.430
So who's the car owner?

275
26:16.513 --> 26:18.015
Min Junho.

276
26:19.766 --> 26:20.809
The doctor.

277
26:42.789 --> 26:46.293
[♪ ominous music playing]

278
26:55.969 --> 26:56.970
[sighs]

279
27:11.568 --> 27:13.528
[♪ sinister music plays]

280
27:37.177 --> 27:39.346
[Jeongmi crying] I feel like it has to be done.

281
27:40.263 --> 27:42.557
I have to do it for my friend Eunhye.

282
27:43.433 --> 27:44.434
[sniffles]

283
27:45.769 --> 27:48.313
It's the anniversary of her death in two days.

284
27:58.448 --> 27:59.574
[exclaims]

285
28:01.243 --> 28:02.452
[Junho] I'll take that.

286
28:16.633 --> 28:18.093
[car door closes]

287
28:27.519 --> 28:28.603
[car door closes]

288
28:29.938 --> 28:31.648
[car starts]

289
28:54.463 --> 28:55.797
[Jisun] Oh.

290
28:57.340 --> 28:58.341
Sir, wait!

291
29:00.635 --> 29:03.597
[♪ ethereal music plays]

292
29:21.490 --> 29:23.742
[♪ music intensifies]

293
29:40.759 --> 29:43.637
[♪ somber music plays]

294
30:00.487 --> 30:02.030
[water running]

295
30:02.906 --> 30:03.990
[water stops]

296
30:07.619 --> 30:10.288
We agreed we'd go to Sangcheon together.

297
30:13.583 --> 30:16.378
I think I rushed you into making that decision.

298
30:19.089 --> 30:21.550
I don't have any reason to go there.

299
30:24.010 --> 30:26.638
It's okay. Take your time to think about it.

300
30:26.721 --> 30:29.474
You can just talk to the police over the phone too.

301
30:29.558 --> 30:33.895
I do feel terrible about what you say happened to you,

302
30:33.979 --> 30:36.189
whether it's true or not.

303
30:36.940 --> 30:40.318
But what happened to you and what happened to me aren't the same.

304
30:45.532 --> 30:47.617
Did something happen?

305
30:49.703 --> 30:53.748
Everything I told you the other day…

306
30:55.208 --> 30:58.170
was a lie.

307
31:00.005 --> 31:01.006
I'm sorry.

308
31:02.924 --> 31:04.843
I hated myself for getting drunk

309
31:04.926 --> 31:07.554
and making that mistake with my friend's husband,

310
31:07.637 --> 31:10.056
then losing my friend.

311
31:12.475 --> 31:14.186
I wanted to ease some of the guilt--

312
31:14.269 --> 31:16.521
This isn't how you were the other day.

313
31:16.605 --> 31:20.233
You knew exactly how dangerous and evil Min Junho was.

314
31:20.317 --> 31:22.527
-So why are you suddenly… -[phone buzzing]

315
31:22.611 --> 31:24.863
-[gasps] Oh, gosh. -[♪ unsettling music plays]

316
31:25.906 --> 31:27.866
Oh, yes, Junho.

317
31:29.159 --> 31:30.952
Sorry to keep you waiting.

318
31:31.036 --> 31:33.705
Could you and Eunhye's mother wait in the car?

319
31:35.290 --> 31:37.626
Okay. I'll be right out.

320
31:39.336 --> 31:40.170
[call disconnects]

321
31:40.253 --> 31:41.296
I have to go.

322
31:45.342 --> 31:47.260
You're afraid of Min Junho, aren't you?

323
31:50.639 --> 31:54.059
What are you talking about?

324
31:56.019 --> 31:58.438
Junho is a good person.

325
31:59.564 --> 32:02.651
I was the one who developed feelings for him.

326
32:04.653 --> 32:05.946
I kept pursuing him.

327
32:07.948 --> 32:10.700
I'm the one who caused him to make that mistake.

328
32:15.288 --> 32:19.376
Can you swear to that in front of Ms. Joo Eunhye?

329
32:24.172 --> 32:27.801
You're incredibly rude and invasive.

330
32:28.802 --> 32:31.930
Stop harassing people who just want to be left alone.

331
32:33.056 --> 32:34.307
Before I call the police.

332
32:34.891 --> 32:36.184
Jeongmi.

333
32:43.066 --> 32:44.818
It wasn't your fault.

334
32:48.196 --> 32:50.991
[♪ music intensifies]

335
32:51.074 --> 32:52.325
[sniffles]

336
33:02.377 --> 33:04.629
[announcement on PA] Attention, please.

337
33:05.630 --> 33:11.011
Flight 7C55 to Sangcheon has been canceled due to weather conditions.

338
33:12.053 --> 33:14.180
Once again,

339
33:14.764 --> 33:20.603
flight 7C55 to Sangcheon has been canceled due to weather conditions.

340
33:20.687 --> 33:23.440
-We apologize for the inconvenience. -[thunderclap]

341
33:23.523 --> 33:25.233
Thank you.

342
33:25.317 --> 33:27.068
[in English] Attention, please…

343
33:30.822 --> 33:33.074
WHITE PSYCHIATRIC CLINIC

344
33:34.659 --> 33:36.661
[psychiatrist, in Korean] It's been three years already.

345
33:38.330 --> 33:40.373
And yet here I am, still a mess.

346
33:41.082 --> 33:42.208
What's wrong with me?

347
33:44.002 --> 33:47.630
Even when I try to make a fresh start, I end up with some attention seeker.

348
33:47.714 --> 33:50.050
I keep telling you, it's not your fault.

349
33:50.133 --> 33:53.136
Sometimes… [exhales] I think…

350
33:55.805 --> 33:57.474
"I don't want to live anymore."

351
33:58.516 --> 33:59.934
"I miss Eunhye."

352
34:04.105 --> 34:06.066
Will a two-week prescription be enough?

353
34:08.735 --> 34:09.778
[mouse clicks]

354
34:11.112 --> 34:12.697
I'll need a medical certificate too.

355
34:14.616 --> 34:16.868
HOTEL PARKING ENTRANCE KEEP ENTRANCE AND EXIT CLEAR

356
34:19.621 --> 34:21.247
[psychiatrist] You're going to sue that woman?

357
34:23.458 --> 34:24.459
Yeah.

358
34:26.127 --> 34:28.963
Make sure you're legally covered to avoid problems down the road.

359
34:30.507 --> 34:32.425
[♪ smooth jazz playing]

360
34:32.509 --> 34:33.843
[host] Welcome.

361
34:33.927 --> 34:35.178
Are you with a party?

362
34:35.804 --> 34:37.097
No, it's just me.

363
34:37.180 --> 34:40.016
[host] In that case, would you mind sitting at the bar?

364
34:40.100 --> 34:41.351
Not at all.

365
34:41.434 --> 34:42.477
[host] Great. Right this way.

366
35:07.210 --> 35:08.336
[bartender] What can I get you?

367
35:09.504 --> 35:10.630
A dark beer, please.

368
35:10.714 --> 35:12.215
[bartender] Sure.

369
35:12.298 --> 35:13.299
[Jisun] Oh.

370
35:15.301 --> 35:16.845
I'll just have one of these.

371
35:16.928 --> 35:18.304
[bartender] Sure, okay.

372
35:20.598 --> 35:21.599
[Jisun sighs]

373
35:29.816 --> 35:31.526
[bartender] Here you go.

374
35:32.235 --> 35:33.236
[stammers]

375
35:37.741 --> 35:40.368
I guess we can just switch ourselves.

376
35:40.452 --> 35:42.036
Okay.

377
35:47.792 --> 35:49.669
I've been coming here for over three years,

378
35:50.462 --> 35:52.297
and they still don't know what I drink.

379
36:04.392 --> 36:05.643
[Jisun exhales deeply]

380
36:11.775 --> 36:12.776
Excuse…

381
36:13.485 --> 36:14.736
Excuse me…

382
36:16.362 --> 36:18.573
-[loudly] We'd like to order, please! -[bartender] Oh, yes.

383
36:22.744 --> 36:24.120
What can I get you?

384
36:24.204 --> 36:25.955
I'll have another one of these, please.

385
36:26.039 --> 36:27.290
[bartender] Sure.

386
36:35.131 --> 36:37.383
-[bartender] Here you go. -Thank you.

387
36:52.607 --> 36:53.733
If it's okay with you,

388
36:54.692 --> 36:57.779
would you like me to recommend a good hangover soup place nearby?

389
37:08.122 --> 37:10.375
[♪ mellow music plays]

390
37:12.085 --> 37:14.587
[no audible dialogue]

391
37:19.592 --> 37:22.387
[♪ music continues]

392
37:26.724 --> 37:28.476
Want another drink?

393
37:28.560 --> 37:29.936
This one's on me.

394
37:30.770 --> 37:32.146
No, actually…

395
37:33.064 --> 37:36.067
How about we share a bottle of wine?

396
37:41.698 --> 37:43.700
[♪ dissonant music plays]

397
37:47.912 --> 37:49.789
[♪ ambient music plays]

398
37:49.873 --> 37:51.040
I should get going.

399
37:52.000 --> 37:53.376
What?

400
37:53.459 --> 37:56.004
-Wait, how about a glass of-- -I said no.

401
38:07.599 --> 38:08.600
[person] Hey.

402
38:12.145 --> 38:13.146
-Hey. -[gasps]

403
38:14.022 --> 38:15.356
Hey, wait.

404
38:16.608 --> 38:18.067
Wait! Hey.

405
38:20.153 --> 38:21.237
[zipper opens]

406
38:21.321 --> 38:23.281
-Wait-- -Don't touch me!

407
38:23.364 --> 38:25.366
[Jisun panting]

408
38:34.459 --> 38:37.587
You left your phone.

409
39:06.366 --> 39:07.867
[phone buzzing]

410
39:16.376 --> 39:17.502
Hello?

411
39:20.463 --> 39:22.715
[staff member] This is the Forensic Science Department at the NFS.

412
39:24.050 --> 39:26.260
The GHB test you requested…

413
39:28.179 --> 39:29.389
We have the results, and…

414
39:29.472 --> 39:31.849
4. RESULTS OF ANALYSIS GAMMA-HYDROXYBUTYRIC ACID, GHB

415
39:31.933 --> 39:32.976
POSITIVE

416
39:33.059 --> 39:34.310
It came back positive.

417
39:38.648 --> 39:40.400
[person on PA] Hello, ladies and gentlemen.

418
39:41.734 --> 39:46.239
-This is your captain, Kang Ilcheon. -[person exclaims]

419
39:47.615 --> 39:50.284
[Ilcheon] Thank you for flying with us on Air Donghae Flight 701

420
39:50.368 --> 39:52.161
to Sangcheon Airport.

421
39:54.122 --> 39:56.249
The weather in Sangcheon is currently clear,

422
39:56.332 --> 39:59.085
with a temperature of 25 degrees Celsius.

423
39:59.168 --> 40:04.007
The weather in Sangcheon is expected to remain mild today,

424
40:04.090 --> 40:05.925
but unexpected changes in air currents

425
40:06.009 --> 40:08.136
-may cause severe turbulence. -[person exclaims]

426
40:09.303 --> 40:10.722
What a coincidence.

427
40:11.431 --> 40:13.307
Well, I guess not.

428
40:13.391 --> 40:16.894
We did both say we were going to Sangcheon.

429
40:20.982 --> 40:22.358
If you're uncomfortable,

430
40:23.443 --> 40:26.446
should I ask to switch seats?

431
40:28.906 --> 40:30.658
No, it's fine. You can stay.

432
40:37.123 --> 40:39.000
[overhead chime]

433
40:43.880 --> 40:44.964
[person] It was good, right?

434
40:46.132 --> 40:47.133
Sorry?

435
40:49.218 --> 40:50.887
The hangover soup place.

436
40:53.598 --> 40:57.185
-I didn't have time to go. -Ah.

437
40:59.729 --> 41:02.648
Well, next time you're there, you should definitely try it.

438
41:02.732 --> 41:04.150
You won't regret it.

439
41:07.904 --> 41:08.905
Okay.

440
41:15.036 --> 41:16.037
You know,

441
41:17.205 --> 41:19.290
I'm not usually like that.

442
41:21.793 --> 41:22.794
Sorry?

443
41:23.920 --> 41:24.921
I just…

444
41:26.005 --> 41:29.675
don't want you to think I'm some kind of creep.

445
41:31.844 --> 41:33.137
I don't normally

446
41:34.305 --> 41:40.186
ask women I just met at a bar to have a drink with me.

447
41:40.269 --> 41:42.563
That's really not who I am.

448
41:44.107 --> 41:46.442
Ah. Okay.

449
41:48.194 --> 41:50.905
I don't know if I should ask you this, but…

450
41:52.657 --> 41:56.244
was it because you have a boyfriend?

451
42:00.498 --> 42:03.167
No, but…

452
42:06.587 --> 42:07.630
Ah.

453
42:10.049 --> 42:11.592
It's okay. Really.

454
42:15.012 --> 42:17.306
Could you, then…

455
42:18.474 --> 42:21.102
give me some advice?

456
42:21.978 --> 42:23.688
What did I do to put you off?

457
42:23.771 --> 42:25.523
You didn't do anything wrong.

458
42:28.151 --> 42:29.610
It's just…

459
42:32.405 --> 42:35.032
I'm just not in a position to date anyone right now.

460
42:44.542 --> 42:47.336
I don't know what you're going through…

461
42:50.840 --> 42:54.886
but I hope everything works out for you.

462
42:57.138 --> 42:58.264
Thank you.

463
43:02.560 --> 43:04.812
-[plane rumbling] -[gasps]

464
43:05.897 --> 43:07.231
[alert chiming]

465
43:08.482 --> 43:10.484
-[♪ ominous music plays] -[passengers murmuring]

466
43:22.663 --> 43:24.832
[Jisun] Have you ever been through something like this?

467
43:29.462 --> 43:31.005
Something happens,

468
43:32.173 --> 43:34.258
and overnight,

469
43:34.342 --> 43:36.177
it's like your whole world has changed.

470
43:39.805 --> 43:41.515
You didn't do anything wrong,

471
43:42.600 --> 43:44.644
but somehow you're the one everyone shuts out.

472
43:47.104 --> 43:48.773
You don't know what to do…

473
43:50.775 --> 43:55.321
and you have no idea how to get back to the way things were before.

474
44:00.034 --> 44:03.204
It might be better to accept your new reality sooner rather than later…

475
44:05.581 --> 44:09.001
-and learn to adjust to it. -You're telling me to just accept it?

476
44:13.381 --> 44:16.175
I found that the more I tried to go back to the way things were…

477
44:18.052 --> 44:19.762
the more it hurt.

478
44:25.768 --> 44:27.728
[♪ calm music plays]

479
44:27.812 --> 44:29.563
It's better to make your new reality…

480
44:31.607 --> 44:34.235
feel as familiar as you can.

481
44:37.363 --> 44:40.449
Because familiarity gives you a sense of security.

482
44:47.832 --> 44:50.710
It's the least painful way

483
44:52.044 --> 44:54.213
to recover as quickly as possible.

484
45:22.700 --> 45:24.577
[Jisun] Well, then, take care.

485
45:27.580 --> 45:28.581
Wait.

486
45:33.169 --> 45:34.587
Do you want to grab a bite?

487
45:40.343 --> 45:42.511
Let me treat you to dinner.

488
45:42.595 --> 45:44.347
When are you free?

489
45:44.430 --> 45:46.349
[♪ unsettling music plays]

490
45:57.485 --> 45:58.819
Why me?

491
46:06.660 --> 46:10.122
I just thought it'd be nice to have a meal together.

492
46:11.248 --> 46:12.625
And after that?

493
46:20.174 --> 46:23.886
If you're not interested, you can just say no.

494
46:27.139 --> 46:28.140
Well, then…

495
46:29.975 --> 46:31.185
Take care.

496
46:44.698 --> 46:46.700
[team leader, muffled] So I told her to invite her friends,

497
46:46.784 --> 46:50.287
and she asked if they couldn't just hang out by themselves.

498
46:50.371 --> 46:52.540
Basically, she just wanted my credit card.

499
46:52.623 --> 46:54.041
So you know what I told her?

500
46:54.583 --> 46:58.587
"Sweetheart, family dinner comes first."

501
47:02.883 --> 47:04.009
Inspector Lee.

502
47:04.844 --> 47:05.845
Yes, sir.

503
47:05.928 --> 47:06.971
You okay?

504
47:07.763 --> 47:08.764
Yes.

505
47:10.766 --> 47:12.017
Why are you looking at that?

506
47:13.727 --> 47:15.146
I have to testify in court.

507
47:15.855 --> 47:17.565
Oh, that's right.

508
47:19.483 --> 47:22.361
[sighs] Kids these days are scarier than adults, huh?

509
47:24.488 --> 47:27.700
So, you're telling me it's just because of the case?

510
47:31.120 --> 47:33.289
You seem like your mind's somewhere else today.

511
47:34.457 --> 47:36.542
If GHB was detected,

512
47:37.918 --> 47:40.129
we have to find out who did it.

513
47:41.505 --> 47:43.424
Even if the circumstances point to someone,

514
47:43.507 --> 47:45.634
we still need proof that it was that person.

515
47:48.971 --> 47:50.097
[sighs]

516
47:52.892 --> 47:53.934
Never mind.

517
47:57.396 --> 47:59.482
-[tapping] -[team leader] Inspector Lee.

518
48:00.357 --> 48:04.069
You know you can talk to me about anything, right?

519
48:04.820 --> 48:07.948
What's gotten into you all of a sudden? You're making me uncomfortable.

520
48:17.458 --> 48:18.751
-[phone chimes] -Huh?

521
48:32.640 --> 48:34.099
[officer] This is Sangcheon Police.

522
48:34.183 --> 48:38.020
A complaint has been filed against you for false accusation and defamation.

523
48:38.103 --> 48:40.064
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

524
48:44.360 --> 48:46.362
[breathing heavily]

525
48:54.703 --> 48:56.247
[door unlocks]

526
49:02.253 --> 49:04.046
How dare you file a complaint against me?

527
49:05.839 --> 49:08.884
You're only making things worse for yourself by doing this here.

528
49:09.802 --> 49:11.762
If you need a lawyer, I can recommend one.

529
49:11.845 --> 49:13.597
Defamation?

530
49:13.681 --> 49:14.974
False accusation?

531
49:15.057 --> 49:17.226
You have the nerve to do this after what you did?

532
49:17.309 --> 49:18.686
I've been falsely accused.

533
49:18.769 --> 49:20.437
I can't just let that go.

534
49:21.814 --> 49:23.148
"Falsely accused"?

535
49:24.692 --> 49:27.111
Have you ever been honest with anyone in your life?

536
49:31.282 --> 49:33.200
I understand how you feel.

537
49:34.326 --> 49:36.453
And I know what you think of me.

538
49:43.836 --> 49:44.837
So?

539
49:45.838 --> 49:47.089
What are you going to do?

540
49:48.382 --> 49:50.342
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

541
49:59.893 --> 50:03.897
Honestly, don't you just want to put an end to all this…

542
50:05.566 --> 50:08.068
and go back to living a quiet, normal life like before?

543
50:10.237 --> 50:11.238
Hmm?

544
50:12.489 --> 50:13.616
You should go back.

545
50:15.242 --> 50:16.327
To the way things were.

546
50:17.745 --> 50:18.746
Hmm?

547
50:22.583 --> 50:24.418
I'll give you a chance to start over.

548
50:27.338 --> 50:28.672
It's easier than you think.

549
50:30.382 --> 50:32.092
All you have to do

550
50:32.176 --> 50:34.511
is post that you made the whole thing up to frame me.

551
50:35.804 --> 50:39.725
With sincere remorse and an apology.

552
50:42.019 --> 50:44.355
You want me to lie for you?

553
50:49.902 --> 50:52.988
Is this how you threatened and manipulated Kim Jeongmi too?

554
50:55.866 --> 50:58.619
I'm never going to give in.

555
51:01.747 --> 51:02.748
You…

556
51:04.208 --> 51:08.253
disrespected me and tarnished my reputation.

557
51:17.721 --> 51:19.014
So that's what this is about.

558
51:24.019 --> 51:25.521
You rapist!

559
51:26.897 --> 51:29.733
Min Junho is a rapist! [screams]

560
51:34.947 --> 51:38.075
Why don't we go inside instead of doing this out here?

561
51:38.826 --> 51:39.993
[screaming]

562
51:41.578 --> 51:42.871
[yelps]

563
51:44.456 --> 51:45.457
[gagging]

564
51:49.002 --> 51:50.212
Keep quiet,

565
51:51.255 --> 51:54.633
or you'll disappear right here.

566
52:04.893 --> 52:06.395
[breathing heavily]

567
52:24.246 --> 52:26.540
[♪ tense music plays]

568
52:35.174 --> 52:37.134
[breathing heavily]

569
52:46.810 --> 52:48.812
DNA ANALYSIS RESULTS NOTICE

570
52:56.695 --> 52:57.821
[sighs]

571
53:02.743 --> 53:06.497
THE DNA PROFILE OF THE VICTIM, LEE HWAYOUNG, WAS DETECTED,

572
53:06.580 --> 53:09.708
AND NO OTHER DNA PROFILES WERE DETECTED

573
53:09.792 --> 53:11.502
SANGCHEON POLICE STATION

574
53:11.585 --> 53:12.586
[Hwayoung] Ma'am.

575
53:13.253 --> 53:14.296
[parent] Detective.

576
53:14.379 --> 53:16.924
Can't you testify without my son?

577
53:18.759 --> 53:20.636
What do you mean?

578
53:23.388 --> 53:25.224
[parent] My son…

579
53:25.307 --> 53:26.642
I think he's scared.

580
53:27.434 --> 53:30.813
We don't know when those guys might come after him again.

581
53:35.192 --> 53:37.027
Let me talk to him.

582
53:41.448 --> 53:42.699
Hi, Chowon.

583
53:45.786 --> 53:47.079
Are you upset?

584
53:53.710 --> 53:55.587
You don't think you can testify?

585
54:02.761 --> 54:03.762
No.

586
54:11.436 --> 54:13.772
Remember what you told me before?

587
54:15.440 --> 54:17.568
You asked me to make sure those guys were caught.

588
54:19.736 --> 54:21.905
So they could never do something like that again.

589
54:25.617 --> 54:27.661
Do you remember what I told you then?

590
54:30.038 --> 54:31.331
[♪ soft music plays]

591
54:31.415 --> 54:32.708
I told you…

592
54:35.544 --> 54:37.754
that you had to be brave…

593
54:40.465 --> 54:42.301
if you wanted them to be punished.

594
54:45.429 --> 54:47.389
If you don't say anything…

595
54:50.809 --> 54:53.145
and keep what happened to yourself…

596
54:56.857 --> 54:58.817
you might regret it someday.

597
55:04.823 --> 55:06.450
Are you okay?

598
55:12.831 --> 55:18.629
dr.min.jh MIN JUNHO

599
55:27.346 --> 55:29.014
[♪ stirring music plays]

600
55:31.016 --> 55:33.477
CAPTAIN

601
55:40.817 --> 55:42.110
[sighs]

602
55:55.040 --> 55:56.041
CALLING KANG JISUN

603
55:56.124 --> 55:57.793
[call connects]

604
56:00.921 --> 56:03.882
[automated voice] The call cannot be connected.

605
56:03.965 --> 56:06.551
Please leave a message after the beep.

606
56:10.305 --> 56:12.015
[call connects]

607
56:12.557 --> 56:14.142
[line ringing]

608
56:14.226 --> 56:16.019
[team leader] Hey, Inspector Lee. What's up?

609
56:16.645 --> 56:17.938
[Hwayoung] Sir.

610
56:19.523 --> 56:21.775
There's something important I need to tell you.

611
56:26.488 --> 56:30.117
[team leader] Let's arrest him today. Let's throw that bastard in jail.

612
56:33.495 --> 56:35.539
We need to be extremely thorough first.

613
56:36.623 --> 56:38.125
If we fail to get him again…

614
56:39.668 --> 56:40.961
[team leader groans]

615
56:41.920 --> 56:47.467
A positive GHB test alone doesn't prove that bastard gave it to you.

616
56:47.551 --> 56:49.636
We need to dig up circumstantial evidence.

617
56:49.720 --> 56:52.931
We need his call records and the location data from his car too.

618
56:53.014 --> 56:54.141
I'll put in the requests.

619
56:54.224 --> 56:56.309
I'll give them hell until they take care of it.

620
56:59.312 --> 57:01.898
-Thank you for meeting me today. -[team leader] And this case…

621
57:03.525 --> 57:05.318
I'll take the lead on the investigation.

622
57:06.987 --> 57:09.489
[sighs] I knew something felt off about that bastard

623
57:09.573 --> 57:11.324
from the moment I saw his face.

624
57:13.660 --> 57:14.953
[sighs]

625
57:17.664 --> 57:19.040
As for my husband…

626
57:22.169 --> 57:23.670
Please don't tell him.

627
57:26.131 --> 57:29.176
[sighs] I guess Seokgu doesn't know.

628
57:29.843 --> 57:31.678
Just until we solve the case.

629
57:33.722 --> 57:34.723
[team leader] Okay.

630
57:37.726 --> 57:39.519
We're going to get that bastard.

631
57:41.897 --> 57:44.649
[♪ lively music plays]

632
57:55.535 --> 57:56.703
[person shouts]

633
57:58.747 --> 57:59.956
-[patron] What the… -[patron 2] Oh, my gosh.

634
58:00.040 --> 58:01.792
-[patrons murmuring] -[patron 3] Oh, no. Is she hurt?

635
58:01.875 --> 58:03.502
-She's had way too much to drink. -[groans]

636
58:04.711 --> 58:05.879
[patron] Excuse me.

637
58:13.762 --> 58:14.971
[Jisun] I'm sorry.

638
58:19.059 --> 58:20.101
[scoffs]

639
58:24.397 --> 58:25.398
[Jisun groans]

640
58:26.358 --> 58:27.901
You said you wanted to start over.

641
58:30.278 --> 58:31.696
Have you given up on everything?

642
58:37.786 --> 58:38.954
[Junho sighs]

643
58:41.790 --> 58:43.625
Where are you going? We need to talk.

644
58:46.378 --> 58:47.379
You're drunk.

645
58:53.343 --> 58:55.220
[Jisun yelling] Min Junho!

646
58:56.137 --> 58:57.347
[patrons murmuring]

647
58:58.265 --> 59:00.725
Min Junho!

648
59:06.356 --> 59:07.357
Make your choice.

649
59:08.024 --> 59:10.527
Either keep quiet or end it here.

650
59:10.610 --> 59:12.445
I won't need a lawyer.

651
59:18.743 --> 59:20.120
You win.

652
59:22.914 --> 59:24.374
I give up.

653
59:27.085 --> 59:30.964
I'll do whatever you want, whatever you tell me to.

654
59:32.048 --> 59:34.259
So please, just let me live.

655
59:42.934 --> 59:44.311
You'd better keep your word.

656
59:51.067 --> 59:52.527
[glasses clink]

657
59:52.611 --> 59:54.362
Sure thing.

658
01:00:08.418 --> 01:00:09.711
[Jisun] Damn it…

659
01:00:12.923 --> 01:00:14.174
[sighs]

660
01:00:20.472 --> 01:00:22.682
[Jisun mumbling] Damn it, where are my keys?

661
01:00:23.266 --> 01:00:24.643
[Jisun hums]

662
01:00:27.020 --> 01:00:28.188
[Junho] You're going to drive?

663
01:00:28.271 --> 01:00:29.272
[Jisun] Not your business.

664
01:00:32.692 --> 01:00:34.069
[Jisun groans]

665
01:00:37.197 --> 01:00:38.365
[car chirps]

666
01:00:47.999 --> 01:00:49.876
I can't, but you can, right?

667
01:00:52.212 --> 01:00:54.047
-What? -Give me a ride.

668
01:00:59.219 --> 01:01:00.971
Don't you know what kind of person I am?

669
01:01:02.806 --> 01:01:04.975
You're the one who called me a criminal.

670
01:01:05.058 --> 01:01:06.935
Yeah, but you know what?

671
01:01:07.978 --> 01:01:10.230
I'm not scared of you at all.

672
01:01:12.065 --> 01:01:13.066
What about you?

673
01:01:14.818 --> 01:01:17.570
You're scared of women.

674
01:01:18.947 --> 01:01:19.948
[sighs]

675
01:01:20.031 --> 01:01:22.325
What the heck made you this way?

676
01:01:24.494 --> 01:01:27.789
Were you starved for affection as a kid?

677
01:01:27.872 --> 01:01:29.165
Were you abused?

678
01:01:33.336 --> 01:01:34.337
Just go home quietly.

679
01:01:34.879 --> 01:01:36.464
And what if I don't?

680
01:01:36.548 --> 01:01:38.341
[Junho grunts, groans]

681
01:01:42.012 --> 01:01:43.847
I told you to just go!

682
01:01:46.266 --> 01:01:47.851
[groans]

683
01:01:50.812 --> 01:01:52.439
[♪ tense music plays]

684
01:02:02.365 --> 01:02:03.825
[groans]

685
01:02:05.702 --> 01:02:07.871
What the…

686
01:02:09.581 --> 01:02:11.041
What's wrong?

687
01:02:11.750 --> 01:02:13.043
Are you okay?

688
01:02:20.175 --> 01:02:21.176
You…

689
01:02:24.971 --> 01:02:28.308
[♪ ominous music plays]

690
01:02:34.939 --> 01:02:38.860
THE PERFECT LIE

691
01:03:02.967 --> 01:03:04.928
-[restraints clanking] -[grunting]

692
01:03:05.011 --> 01:03:07.555
I'm not going to make the same mistake this time.

693
01:03:08.389 --> 01:03:10.934
So this time, I'm going to be the one lying.

694
01:03:11.017 --> 01:03:13.603
[Hyunsoo] What if I tell them I was with you that day, Dad?

695
01:03:13.686 --> 01:03:16.064
How do you know your dad didn't go out?

696
01:03:16.147 --> 01:03:18.900
I can't make you lie too.

697
01:03:18.983 --> 01:03:21.319
I guess the investigation isn't going so well again.

698
01:03:21.402 --> 01:03:23.530
You don't need to know everything about my work.

699
01:03:23.613 --> 01:03:26.116
[Jisun] Min Junho isn't going to just let this go.

700
01:03:26.199 --> 01:03:28.451
He'll find some way to get back at me.

701
01:03:35.917 --> 01:03:38.044
[♪ unsettling music plays]

702
01:03:46.177 --> 01:03:47.762
THE PERFECT LIE

703
01:03:47.846 --> 01:03:49.848
Translated by Liya Hyunjoo Choi
